PROJECT REPORT
Latest Movies Dataset Analysis (2025)
Data Analysis using Python, Pandas, Matplotlib and Jupyter Notebook
1. Abstract
This project performs exploratory data analysis on a dataset of latest movies around the year 2025. The analysis examines movie release dates, original languages, popularity, ratings, and vote counts. Python is used in a Jupyter Notebook to load, clean, transform, analyze, and visualize the data. The project focuses on understanding how release month and original language relate to movie popularity and ratings, and on examining the relationship between popularity and ratings.
2. Introduction
Movie datasets contain useful information that can be analyzed to discover patterns in audience interest and movie performance. This project uses the file 'Latest 2025 Movies Datasets.csv' and analyzes the columns title, release_date, original_language, popularity, vote_average, and vote_count.
3. Problem Statement
The project aims to understand whether movie popularity and ratings vary according to release month and original language, and whether highly rated movies are necessarily highly popular.
4. Research Question
How do the release month and original language affect movie popularity and ratings, and what is the relationship between popularity and ratings?
5. Objectives
•	Load and inspect the movie dataset.
•	Check data types, missing values, and basic statistics.
•	Convert release dates into a proper datetime format.
•	Extract year and month from the release date.
•	Clean rows with missing release date, popularity, or rating values.
•	Analyze movie popularity and rating distributions.
•	Analyze the number of movies by original language.
•	Compare average ratings across commonly represented languages.
•	Compare average popularity and movie counts across release months.
•	Study the relationship between popularity and ratings using correlation and visualizations.
•	Identify highly popular and highly rated movies using the available vote-count filter.
